{"id":"2cf9195e036cacdd4bede10f9ecddec09d71f3c7","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/airflow","sha":"2cf9195e036cacdd4bede10f9ecddec09d71f3c7","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"airflow-core/docs/core-concepts/auth-manager/index.rst","lines":["@@ -130,9 +130,10 @@ Each advertised grant must follow the contract below, so that clients work with"," to ``token_endpoint`` returns ``201`` with ``{\"access_token\": ...}``, valid for ``[api_auth] jwt_cli_expiration_time``."," "," * ``password``: the client sends ``username`` and ``password``. This is the default when ``grant_type`` is omitted.","-* ``authorization_code``: the browser opens ``authorization_endpoint`` with ``redirect_uri`` (``http`` loopback","-  only), ``state`` and a required ``S256`` ``code_challenge``. The client then sends ``code``, ``code_verifier`` and","-  ``redirect_uri``.","+* ``authorization_code``: the browser opens ``authorization_endpoint`` with ``redirect_uri``, ``state`` and a","+  required ``S256`` ``code_challenge``. ``redirect_uri`` must be ``http://127.0.0.1:<port>/callback`` or","+  ``http://[::1]:<port>/callback``, with any port, so admins can register one fixed URI in the identity provider.","+  The client then sends ``code``, ``code_verifier`` and ``redirect_uri``."," * ``urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code``: ``device_authorization_endpoint`` returns the RFC 8628 fields.","   The client polls with ``device_code``, and gets ``400`` with ``authorization_pending`` or ``slow_down`` until the","   user approves."],"additions":4,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/README.rst","lines":["@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ PIP package                                 Version required"," ==========================================  =================="," ``apache-airflow``                          ``>=3.0.0``"," ``apache-airflow-providers-common-compat``  ``>=1.18.0``","-``python-keycloak``                         ``>=5.0.0``","+``python-keycloak``                         ``>=5.12.0``"," ==========================================  =================="," "," The changelog for the provider package can be found in the"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/docs/auth-manager/token.rst","lines":["@@ -30,7 +30,11 @@ Several endpoints exist to create tokens depending on the authentication method"," If a user or service needs to interact with the Airflow public API, they can create a token using their credentials."," "," - ``/auth/token``: Create token using username and password, client credentials, or a Keycloak-issued JWT assertion, with a ``[config][api_auth]jwt_expiration_time`` expiration time.","-- ``/auth/token/cli``: Create token for Airflow CLI using username and password with a ``[config][api_auth]jwt_cli_expiration_time`` expiration time.","+- ``/auth/token/cli``: Create token for command-line clients such as ``airflowctl``, with a ``[config][api_auth]jwt_cli_expiration_time`` expiration time.","+  Besides username and password, it supports token refresh and browser login, see :ref:`keycloak-cli-browser-login`.","+","+Both endpoints return ``503`` when Keycloak cannot be reached or answers with a server error. The client can try again","+later."," "," "," Example","@@ -135,3 +139,76 @@ token for subsequent public API calls:"," ","     curl -s \"${ENDPOINT_URL}/api/v2/dags\" \\","         -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${AIRFLOW_TOKEN}\"","+","+","+.. _keycloak-cli-browser-login:","+","+Command-line clients","+''''''''''''''''''''","+","+Command-line clients such as ``airflowctl`` get their token from ``/auth/token/cli``. Besides username and password,","+this endpoint offers two more ways to get a token:","+","+- **Refresh**: get fresh Keycloak tokens without logging in again.","+- **Browser login**: log in through Keycloak in the browser. It is turned off by default.","+","+Clients find out which of these the server offers by calling ``GET /api/v2/auth/cli/metadata``.","+","+.. note::","+    The metadata route exists on Airflow 3.5 and later. On earlier versions, refresh and browser login still work","+    when called directly, but clients such as ``airflowctl`` cannot discover them, so they cannot offer browser login.","+","+Refresh","+~~~~~~~","+","+A CLI token contains a Keycloak access token, which usually expires after a few minutes. To keep calling the API, the","+client exchanges its current CLI token for a new one:","+","+.. code-block:: bash","+","+    curl -X 'POST' \\","+        \"${ENDPOINT_URL}/auth/token/cli\" \\","+        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\","+        -d '{\"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"token\": \"<current CLI token>\"}'","+","+The new token:","+","+- never expires later than the current one, so refreshing never extends a session.","+- lasts at most ``[api_auth] jwt_cli_expiration_time``, so refreshing a longer-lived token from ``/auth/token``","+  shortens it.","+- can expire up to a minute earlier than the current one, because its lifetime is rounded down to the minute. These","+  minutes add up, so frequent refreshes end the session sooner.","+","+On Airflow 3.2 and later, the current token is revoked once the new one is issued. Airflow 3.0 and 3.1 cannot revoke","+tokens, so there the current token keeps working until it expires, even after logging out.","+","+A refresh fails with:","+","+- ``403`` when the token is expired or revoked, or the Keycloak session has ended. The user has to log in again.","+- ``400`` when Keycloak issued the token without a refresh token, which happens when \"Use Refresh Tokens\" is turned","+  off in the Keycloak client. The user has to log in again.","+- ``503`` when Keycloak cannot be reached or answers with a server error. The client can try again later. Before","+  Airflow 3.1.7, a server error returns ``403`` instead.","+","+Browser login","+~~~~~~~~~~~~~","+","+Browser login uses the OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow with PKCE. To turn it on:","+","+1. Set ``[keycloak_auth_manager] cli_authorization_code_enabled = True``.","+2. In the Keycloak client, add ``http://127.0.0.1/callback`` and ``http://[::1]/callback`` to the valid redirect","+   URIs. Keycloak ignores the port of loopback redirect URIs, as RFC 8252 requires, so the client can listen on any","+   port.","+3. Leave PKCE turned off in the Keycloak client. Airflow requires it for command-line clients, and turning it on in","+   Keycloak would break the web login, which does not use it.","+","+A login then goes like this:","+","+1. The client listens on ``http://127.0.0.1:<port>/callback`` (or ``[::1]``) and opens ``/auth/login/cli`` in the","+   browser, with ``redirect_uri``, ``state``, ``code_challenge`` and ``code_challenge_method=S256``.","+2. The user logs in to Keycloak, which redirects the browser to the client's callback with ``code`` and ``state``.","+3. The client sends ``grant_type=authorization_code``, ``code``, ``code_verifier`` and ``redirect_uri`` to","+   ``/auth/token/cli``, and gets its CLI token.","+","+Airflow refuses any challenge method other than ``S256``, and any ``redirect_uri`` that is not a loopback callback","+like the one above."],"additions":78,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/docs/index.rst","lines":["@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ PIP package                                 Version required"," ==========================================  =================="," ``apache-airflow``                          ``>=3.0.0``"," ``apache-airflow-providers-common-compat``  ``>=1.18.0``","-``python-keycloak``                         ``>=5.0.0``","+``python-keycloak``                         ``>=5.12.0``"," ==========================================  =================="," "," Downloading official packages"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/provider.yaml","lines":["@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@ config:","         version_added: 0.0.1","         example: ~","         default: ~","+      cli_authorization_code_enabled:","+        description: |","+          Let command-line clients such as ``airflowctl`` log in through the browser","+          (authorization code flow with PKCE). Add ``http://127.0.0.1/callback`` and","+          ``http://[::1]/callback`` to the valid redirect URIs of the Keycloak client. Clients","+          discover this login on Airflow 3.5 and later.","+        type: boolean","+        version_added: 0.14.0","+        example: ~","+        default: \"False\"","       jwt_federated_client_ids:","         description: |","           Comma-separated allow-list of Keycloak client ids (``azp`` claim) permitted to"],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/pyproject.toml","lines":["@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ requires-python = \">=3.11\""," dependencies = [","     \"apache-airflow>=3.0.0\",","     \"apache-airflow-providers-common-compat>=1.18.0\",","-    \"python-keycloak>=5.0.0\",","+    \"python-keycloak>=5.12.0\","," ]"," "," [dependency-groups]"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/src/airflow/providers/keycloak/auth_manager/constants.py","lines":["@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@"," # to use the jwt-bearer grant. Empty/unset denies all callers."," CONF_JWT_FEDERATED_CLIENT_IDS_KEY = \"jwt_federated_client_ids\""," CONF_TEAM_LEVEL_AUTHORIZATION_KEY = \"team_level_authorization\"","+CONF_CLI_AUTHORIZATION_CODE_ENABLED_KEY = \"cli_authorization_code_enabled\""," "," # Extra Cookie names"," COOKIE_NAME_ACCESS_TOKEN = \"_access_token\""],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/src/airflow/providers/keycloak/auth_manager/datamodels/token.py","lines":["@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@"," # under the License."," from __future__ import annotations"," ","-from typing import Annotated, Literal","+from typing import Annotated, Any, Literal"," "," from pydantic import Field, RootModel, model_validator"," ","@@ -26,9 +26,18 @@","     create_client_credentials_token,","     create_jwt_federated_token,","     create_token_for,","+    create_token_from_authorization_code,","+    refresh_cli_token,"," )"," "," ","+def default_to_password_grant(data: Any) -> Any:","+    \"\"\"Add the default ``password`` grant_type, leaving a malformed body to the union.\"\"\"","+    if isinstance(data, dict) and \"grant_type\" not in data:","+        return {**data, \"grant_type\": \"password\"}","+    return data","+","+"," class TokenResponse(BaseModel):","     \"\"\"Token serializer for responses.\"\"\""," ","@@ -82,6 +91,36 @@ def create_token(self, expiration_time_in_seconds: int) -> str:","         )"," "," ","+class TokenRefreshBody(StrictBaseModel):","+    \"\"\"Refresh grant serializer for post bodies; ``token`` is the current CLI token.\"\"\"","+","+    grant_type: Literal[\"refresh_token\"]","+    token: str = Field()","+","+    def create_token(self, expiration_time_in_seconds: int) -> str:","+        \"\"\"Create token from a CLI token that is still valid, expiring no later than it.\"\"\"","+        return refresh_cli_token(self.token, expiration_time_in_seconds=expiration_time_in_seconds)","+","+","+class TokenAuthorizationCodeBody(StrictBaseModel):","+    \"\"\"Authorization code grant serializer for post bodies, used by the browser login of CLI clients.\"\"\"","+","+    grant_type: Literal[\"authorization_code\"]","+    code: str = Field()","+    # RFC 7636 section 4.1 length bounds.","+    code_verifier: str = Field(min_length=43, max_length=128)","+    redirect_uri: str = Field()","+","+    def create_token(self, expiration_time_in_seconds: int) -> str:","+        \"\"\"Create token from an authorization code and its PKCE verifier.\"\"\"","+        return create_token_from_authorization_code(","+            self.code,","+            self.code_verifier,","+            self.redirect_uri,","+            expiration_time_in_seconds=expiration_time_in_seconds,","+        )","+","+"," TokenUnion = Annotated[","     TokenPasswordBody | TokenClientCredentialsBody | TokenJwtFederatedBody,","     Field(discriminator=\"grant_type\"),","@@ -93,8 +132,20 @@ class TokenBody(RootModel[TokenUnion]):"," ","     @model_validator(mode=\"before\")","     @classmethod","-    def default_grant_type(cls, data):","-        \"\"\"Add default grant_type for discrimination.\"\"\"","-        if \"grant_type\" not in data:","-            data[\"grant_type\"] = \"password\"","-        return data","+    def default_grant_type(cls, data: Any) -> Any:","+        return default_to_password_grant(data)","+","+","+TokenCliUnion = Annotated[","+    TokenPasswordBody | TokenRefreshBody | TokenAuthorizationCodeBody,","+    Field(discriminator=\"grant_type\"),","+]","+","+","+class TokenCliBody(RootModel[TokenCliUnion]):","+    \"\"\"Token request body for command-line clients.\"\"\"","+","+    @model_validator(mode=\"before\")","+    @classmethod","+    def default_grant_type(cls, data: Any) -> Any:","+        return default_to_password_grant(data)"],"additions":57,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/src/airflow/providers/keycloak/auth_manager/exceptions.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@","+# Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one","+# or more contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file","+# distributed with this work for additional information","+# regarding copyright ownership.  The ASF licenses this file","+# to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the","+# \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance","+# with the License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at","+#","+#   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0","+#","+# Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing,","+# software distributed under the License is distributed on an","+# \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY","+# KIND, either express or implied.  See the License for the","+# specific language governing permissions and limitations","+# under the License.","+","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+from keycloak import KeycloakConnectionError, KeycloakError","+","+try:","+    from airflow.api_fastapi.auth.managers.exceptions import AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException","+except ImportError:","+","+    class AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException(Exception):  # type: ignore[no-redef]","+        \"\"\"In case it is using a version of Airflow without ``AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException``.\"\"\"","+","+","+def is_keycloak_outage(error: KeycloakError) -> bool:","+    \"\"\"Return whether ``error`` means Keycloak could not be reached or failed on its side.\"\"\"","+    return isinstance(error, KeycloakConnectionError) or (error.response_code or 0) >= 500","+","+","+__all__ = [\"AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException\", \"is_keycloak_outage\"]"],"additions":35,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/src/airflow/providers/keycloak/auth_manager/keycloak_auth_manager.py","lines":["@@ -51,10 +51,17 @@","     from airflow.api_fastapi.auth.managers.base_auth_manager import ResourceMethod as ExtendedResourceMethod"," "," from airflow.api_fastapi.common.types import MenuItem","+","+try:","+    from airflow.api_fastapi.common.types import CliLoginMethods","+except ImportError:","+    # Airflow versions without CLI login discovery never call ``get_cli_login_methods``.","+    CliLoginMethods = None  # type: ignore[assignment,misc]"," from airflow.cli.cli_config import CLICommand"," from airflow.providers.common.compat.sdk import AirflowException, conf"," from airflow.providers.keycloak.auth_manager.cache import single_flight"," from airflow.providers.keycloak.auth_manager.constants import (","+    CONF_CLI_AUTHORIZATION_CODE_ENABLED_KEY,","     CONF_CLIENT_ID_KEY,","     CONF_CLIENT_SECRET_KEY,","     CONF_REALM_KEY,","@@ -109,6 +116,10 @@"," )"," "," ","+def is_cli_authorization_code_enabled() -> bool:","+    return conf.getboolean(CONF_SECTION_NAME, CONF_CLI_AUTHORIZATION_CODE_ENABLED_KEY, fallback=False)","+","+"," class KeycloakAuthManager(BaseAuthManager[KeycloakAuthManagerUser]):","     \"\"\"","     Keycloak auth manager.","@@ -241,6 +252,19 @@ def get_url_logout(self) -> str | None:","         base_url = conf.get(\"api\", \"base_url\", fallback=\"/\")","         return urljoin(base_url, f\"{AUTH_MANAGER_FASTAPI_APP_PREFIX}/logout\")"," ","+    def get_cli_login_methods(self) -> CliLoginMethods:","+        token_endpoint = f\"{AUTH_MANAGER_FASTAPI_APP_PREFIX}/token/cli\"","+        if not is_cli_authorization_code_enabled():","+            return CliLoginMethods(","+                grant_types_supported=[\"password\", \"refresh_token\"], token_endpoint=token_endpoint","+            )","+        return CliLoginMethods(","+            grant_types_supported=[\"password\", \"refresh_token\", \"authorization_code\"],","+            code_challenge_methods_supported=[\"S256\"],","+            authorization_endpoint=f\"{AUTH_MANAGER_FASTAPI_APP_PREFIX}/login/cli\",","+            token_endpoint=token_endpoint,","+        )","+","     def refresh_user(self, *, user: KeycloakAuthManagerUser | None) -> KeycloakAuthManagerUser | None:","         # According to RFC6749 section 4.4.3, a refresh token should not be included when using","         # the Service accounts/client_credentials flow."],"additions":24,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/src/airflow/providers/keycloak/auth_manager/middleware.py","lines":["@@ -32,18 +32,9 @@","     COOKIE_NAME_ACCESS_TOKEN,","     COOKIE_NAME_REFRESH_TOKEN,"," )","+from airflow.providers.keycloak.auth_manager.exceptions import AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException"," from airflow.providers.keycloak.version_compat import AIRFLOW_V_3_1_8_PLUS"," ","-try:","-    from airflow.api_fastapi.auth.managers.exceptions import AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException","-except ImportError:","-","-    class AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException(Exception):  # type: ignore[no-redef]","-        \"\"\"In case it is using a version of Airflow without ``AuthManagerRefreshTokenExpiredException``.\"\"\"","-","-        pass","-","-"," if AIRFLOW_V_3_1_8_PLUS:","     from airflow.api_fastapi.app import get_cookie_path"," else:"],"additions":1,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"providers/keycloak/src/airflow/providers/keycloak/auth_manager/openapi/v2-keycloak-auth-manager-generated.yaml","lines":["@@ -19,6 +19,72 @@ paths:","           content:","             application/json:","               schema: {}","+  /auth/login/cli:","+    get:","+      tags:","+      - KeycloakAuthManagerLogin","+      summary: Login Cli","+      description: Start the browser login of a command-line client.","+      operationId: login_cli","+      parameters:","+      - name: redirect_uri","+        in: query","+        required: true","+        schema:","+          type: string","+          title: Redirect Uri","+      - name: state","+        in: query","+        required: true","+        schema:","+          type: string","+          minLength: 1","+          maxLength: 512","+          title: State","+      - name: code_challenge","+        in: query","+        required: true","+        schema:","+          type: string","+          pattern: ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}$","+          title: Code Challenge","+      - name: code_challenge_method","+        in: query","+        required: true","+        schema:","+          const: S256","+          type: string","+          title: Code Challenge Method","+      responses:","+        '200':","+          description: Successful Response","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema: {}","+        '307':","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema:","+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","+          description: Temporary Redirect","+        '400':","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema:","+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","+          description: Bad Request","+        '503':","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema:","+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","+          description: Service Unavailable","+        '422':","+          description: Validation Error","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema:","+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError'","   /auth/login_callback:","     get:","       tags:","@@ -93,6 +159,12 @@ paths:","             application/json:","               schema:","                 $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","+        '503':","+          description: Service Unavailable","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema:","+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","         '422':","           description: Validation Error","           content:","@@ -109,7 +181,7 @@ paths:","         content:","           application/json:","             schema:","-              $ref: '#/components/schemas/TokenPasswordBody'","+              $ref: '#/components/schemas/TokenCliBody'","         required: true","       responses:","         '201':","@@ -130,6 +202,12 @@ paths:","             application/json:","               schema:","                 $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","+        '503':","+          description: Service Unavailable","+          content:","+            application/json:","+              schema:","+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPExceptionResponse'","         '422':","           description: Validation Error","           content:","@@ -160,6 +238,33 @@ components:","           title: Detail","       type: object","       title: HTTPValidationError","+    TokenAuthorizationCodeBody:","+      properties:","+        grant_type:","+          type: string","+          const: authorization_code","+          title: Grant Type","+        code:","+          type: string","+          title: Code","+        code_verifier:","+          type: string","+          maxLength: 128","+          minLength: 43","+          title: Code Verifier","+        redirect_uri:","+          type: string","+          title: Redirect Uri","+      additionalProperties: false","+      type: object","+      required:","+      - grant_type","+      - code","+      - code_verifier","+      - redirect_uri","+      title: TokenAuthorizationCodeBody","+      description: Authorization code grant serializer for post bodies, used by the","+        browser login of CLI clients.","     TokenBody:","       oneOf:","       - $ref: '#/components/schemas/TokenPasswordBody'","@@ -173,6 +278,19 @@ components:","           client_credentials: '#/components/schemas/TokenClientCredentialsBody'","           password: '#/components/schemas/TokenPasswordBody'","           urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer: '#/components/schemas/TokenJwtFederatedBody'","+    TokenCliBody:","+      oneOf:","+      - $ref: '#/components/schemas/TokenPasswordBody'","+      - $ref: '#/components/schemas/TokenRefreshBody'","+      - $ref: '#/components/schemas/TokenAuthorizationCodeBody'","+      title: TokenCliBody","+      description: Token request body for command-line clients.","+      discriminator:","+        propertyName: grant_type","+        mapping:","+          authorization_code: '#/components/schemas/TokenAuthorizationCodeBody'","+          password: '#/components/schemas/TokenPasswordBody'","+          refresh_token: '#/components/schemas/TokenRefreshBody'","     TokenClientCredentialsBody:","       properties:","         grant_type:","@@ -237,6 +355,23 @@ components:","       - password","       title: TokenPasswordBody","       description: Password grant token serializer for post bodies.","+    TokenRefreshBody:","+      properties:","+        grant_type:","+          type: string","+          const: refresh_token","+          title: Grant Type